From 04df66e712d8ec28da14a81d225386075a157751 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 20:23:14 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] PETSc: copy the matrices of hypre on the host without
 initializing the GPU

MFEM converts a matrix of hypre through the MATHYPRE format of PETSc,
whose creation initializes the GPU when PETSc and hypre are built for it.
The solvers of PETSc compute on the host in mfem-mgis: each process of a
computation on the host thus opened a context on the GPU (262 MiB each with
CUDA 13, 2.1 GiB for 8 processes) and lost 0.4 second at the first setup.
The matrices of hypre are now copied row by row in the AIJ format of the
host (makeHostMatrix), for the Krylov solvers, the preconditioners and
SNES. On the beam of 56,355 unknowns with 8 processes, the first setup
falls from 0.41 to 0.011 second and the following ones from 0.015 to
0.010 second, with the same iterations.

PETScSolversTest and SNESSolverTest check that the GPU is not initialized
when MFEM computes on the host. Rename a parameter which shadowed a member
of PETScOptions.
